    讯 | xùn | interrogate; message; news

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 询问 emphasizes formal, polite, or institutional inquiry into facts, conditions, or expert opinions.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 询问 vs. 问 | wèn | 问 is monosyllabic and colloquial, used for everyday casual asking (问路、问好), whereas 询问 is formal and disyllabic, used in official, medical, or investigative situations.
    2 | 询问 vs. 打听 | dǎtǐng | 询问 carries an objective, transparent, and respectful tone for official or business clarification, while 打听 implies informal gossiping, personal probing, or scouting out private news.
    3 | 询问 vs. 质问 | zhìwèn | 询问 is neutral and courteous seeking genuine information, whereas 质问 is an aggressive, confrontational interrogation demanding an immediate explanation or confession.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 当陌生的白发老人踏入村庄时，见众人扶老携幼惊慌逃离，便温和地上前询问究竟。村民起初畏惧不敢言，但在老人沉静坚定的目光注视下，终于道出了年兽除夕夜下山伤人的古老秘密。 | Dāng mòshēng de báifà lǎorén tàrù cūnzhuāng shí, jiàn zhòngrén fúlǎo-xiéyòu jīnghuāng táolí, biàn wēnhé de shàngqián xúnwèn jiūjìng. Cūnmín qǐchū wèijù bù gǎn yán, dàn zài lǎorén chénjìng jiāndìng de mùguāng zhùshì xià, zhōngyú dàochū le Niánshòu Chúxī yè xiàshān shāngrén de gǔlǎo mìmì. | When the unfamiliar white-haired elder entered the village and saw crowds fleeing in panic with elders and children, he stepped forward gently to inquire about the matter. At first villagers shrank from speaking, but under his calm and resolute gaze, they ultimately revealed the ancient secret of the beast Nian descending on New Year's Eve to harm mortals. | Cuando el forastero de cabellos blancos llegó a la aldea y vio a la gente huir presa del pánico, se acercó a preguntar con serenidad lo que sucedía. Aunque al principio temían hablar, la mirada firme y apacible del anciano los animó a revelar el antiguo secreto de la fiera Nian que bajaba a herir personas en fin de año.
  #2 | 在现代公共治理中，行政机关做出重大民生决策前，必须依法开展深入的民意询问与专家论证。通过规范化制度倾听基层诉求，不仅能够有效规避执行偏差，更能显著提升公共政策的科学性与公信力。 | Zài xiàndài gōnggòng zhìlǐ zhōng, xíngzhèng jīguān zuòchū zhòngdà mínshēng juécè qián, bìxū yīfǎ kāizhǎn shēnrù de mínyì xúnwèn yǔ zhuānjiā lùnzhèng. Tōngguò guīfànhuà zhìdù qīngtīng jīcéng sùqiú, bùjǐn nénggòu yǒuxiào guībì zhíxíng piānchā, gèng néng xiǎnzhù tíshēng gōnggòng zhèngcè de kēxuéxìng yǔ gōngxìnlì. | In contemporary public governance, before administrative organs finalize major welfare decisions, they must conduct thorough public inquiries and expert deliberations according to law. Attending to grassroots appeals through standardized procedures avoids operational missteps and enhances the scientific rigor and credibility of public policies. | En la gestión pública actual, los órganos administrativos deben realizar consultas ciudadanas e informes periciales antes de tomar decisiones sobre el bienestar común. Escuchar las demandas de la sociedad mediante mecanismos normados evita desviaciones y consolida la credibilidad de las políticas públicas.